(PRC-42 — `fork the process` and the reap forms are EXPRESSIONS, not
 statements: they work anywhere an expression is valid, not only after
 `Set`. Here one reap is the subject of an `If` condition and one fork is
 the argument of a function call.
 SAFETY: every child this probe makes is its own and is reaped. A leaf
 must do the same (plan 323 Tier CONFINE: the child must be the program's
 own, and the count bounded).
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-42.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   a reap read directly in a condition
   a fork read as a call argument gave parent
   the child was reaped
)
To 'describe pid' with a number called pid.
    If pid is 0 then, Return a text, "child".
    Return a text, "parent".

If reap process 999999 is less than 0 then, print "a reap read directly in a condition".
a text called role is 'describe pid' of fork the process.
If role is "child" then, Exit 0.
print "a fork read as a call argument gave {role}".
a number called reaped is reap any child process.
If reaped is greater than 0 then, print "the child was reaped".
